  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_9341346411b147f2bda81d7f00ae6bd1",
      "statement": "oauthCmd selects one flow: with a service-account --account file and --jwt it calls DoJWTAuthorization; with a service-account file it calls DoTwoLeggedAuthorization (JWT-bearer grant); --console-flow device or --console selects DoDeviceAuthorization; --console-flow oob selects DoManualAuthorization; otherwise the default is DoLoopbackAuthorization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L495-L509",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53cce19dcc0281811189a0ffa46c55533301f273ff252fd61f23e3d0f2efc238:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_063f6974d5d24a98bc91efcc32886ec0",
      "statement": "DoTwoLeggedAuthorization parses the service account's PKCS#8 private key, signs an RS256 JWT with aud set to the token endpoint, iss set to the account's client_email, and exp now+3600, then posts it with grant_type urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L451-L461",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d167f67244946d015d89d0e460bd21fb59f26b98cfe18c2bc317b284fb9491d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L981-L1042",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a82e82e2466a222e7845b6932b709cad64543312306bdc2ad8473be29f9b01c9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cf280aef68d845a49ad42f381503fb66",
      "statement": "With --jwt, DoJWTAuthorization signs and returns the raw RS256 JWT (exp now+3600) as the token instead of exchanging anything at the token endpoint; the audience parameter is supplied by oauthCmd.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L1044-L1088",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92c6a49bfffe07ef746d8c67ee16aebf7648b573378ae2d70cee2358055a3261:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L496-L500",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:052c3fc24f502fc0952a5ed12a04f011a76cebc391b8edc51f7166f6209bbfc8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_18e9bddacadd4f08a50c149b081e64a7",
      "statement": "The known providers google and github have hard-coded authorization, device-authorization, token, and userinfo endpoints; any other provider must be an https:// URL or validation fails.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L330-L349",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2648622d3267b8311941cf25fb8ec859ccec7dbecf0d30347589dabe57f24614:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L573-L586",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4927c0bf42e4dadf0b17563e2f3ef9f81f34427850660914cfa8a6ca54c6d63a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_76e723fe049c47f3ab7ec38f87f740f5",
      "statement": "For non-known providers, newOauth fetches /.well-known/openid-configuration (OIDC discovery) to resolve the authorization, device-authorization, and token endpoints; explicit --authorization-endpoint and --device-authorization-endpoint flags require --token-endpoint and clear the provider.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L632-L656",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eda34d6b9408a7775b9337fb391cc5c0b9c052860ff93e15bd7f8c2bcac83072:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L684-L709",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d007e267533182b007423b4544bb8f029766221060620af24057f7e0ad8ce4a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6bfaa8fb278a4354a29bca3886327520",
      "statement": "Default Google client IDs are compiled in for the standard flow and the device flow (documented in source as open-source testing clients with no security access); --client-id/--client-secret override them, and a --client-id is required whenever the provider is not the Google default or an authorization endpoint is set.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L397-L403",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4973bd5af6a2f1a6dc0a553c3b481a0e2dd78d6c09c4e6bca0d96b274782874e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L47-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:905fb409c627ccc7117b9a5b1282ae3a077b044ee3ab61268faedf95d6dac813:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f5c0d20a708449ca5de6dfeb84dba9d",
      "statement": "DoLoopbackAuthorization starts a local server (127.0.0.1:0 by default or --listen, with --listen-url overriding the redirect URI), prints or opens the authorize URL, and waits up to 2 minutes for the token or error channel; STEP_OPEN_BROWSER=0 skips opening the browser and prints the URL instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L765-L814",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:da934dee1de07f2e9efc825044763e9d016add12b6d41fc21ac35decb261e19f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c447c478cd4d46ecaefae4dd05c973e3",
      "statement": "The authorization-code request includes response_type=code, random state and nonce, login_hint from --email, scopes (default 'openid email'), prompt, extra auth params, and PKCE S256; the exchange posts the code_verifier with client credentials and redirect_uri.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L1197-L1231",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52b5f48922465ee9e7a2109c23c0937f753b206bf2ddf6dbb2436dd8b07b72cc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L1233-L1255",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca45ad4614e18e1aef80b20428dffea35ecae0efd655815559215476d45e5dcc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7b32e7d74e0f4791b71eada763f5785d",
      "statement": "The callback handler validates the state parameter, exchanges the code, redirects the browser to --redirect-url when set (otherwise renders a success page), and delivers the token over a channel; bad requests render a failure page and send the error to the CLI.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L1090-L1150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:473d71b4f1eca21e206c91cada8467c2c44756d86ec4e73e981445c8aa54bc95:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_42526f7a9ae44b9f8bcd65556789276c",
      "statement": "DoDeviceAuthorization implements RFC 8628: it prefers verification_uri_complete (printing no user code), tolerates Google's non-spec verification_url, defaults the poll interval to 5 seconds, and polls the token endpoint until the token arrives or the grant expires (expires_in, capped at 5 minutes).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L861-L952",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:001b18ef620d5830152c65cd4fc2699a106b198993972600be3c2b9a07aa218c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_401f5c426bb946b883ade0a509bbaeb1",
      "statement": "The OOB flow (DoManualAuthorization) sets redirect_uri to urn:ietf:wg:oauth:2.0:oob, prints the authorize URL, reads the verification code from stdin, and exchanges it at the token endpoint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L62-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33415f8e67893e816a983db4851eb51c03260998559cc58e2b4f57c8e94d4e23:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L816-L846",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:66ab37d3e0f20332730e64eb40ed45dfacd2cfbe84ad72c83f037337b10aefdb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_efbcbfb672e842e6899fbda87f00ec88",
      "statement": "Output modes: --header prints 'Authorization: Bearer <token>', --bare prints only the token, default pretty-prints the token JSON; --oidc selects the OIDC ID token instead of the access token in all modes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L515-L535",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7206bf92c667c345aa7d21972f8997324d954b2876fe7a4169045c19a20e79a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1308f7bc13d5402a952788cf4a1a8ff7",
      "statement": "OIDC provisioners obtain tokens by exec'ing 'step oauth --oidc --bare' with the provisioner's configuration endpoint, client credentials, scopes, auth params, optional --console, and the provisioner listen address (overridable via the STEP_LISTEN environment variable).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_generator.go#L142-L169",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:43aee3bfeceb94b72ab1fe1863abacc5c402470083a34af5626edb0f4d30e4f4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3126cec9c9d84388aa09ff2caea3fb61",
      "statement": "The hidden --implicit flow uses response_type 'id_token token', requires --insecure and --client-id, and uses a JavaScript redirect page to forward the URL fragment back to the callback handler.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L289-L299",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47e47593e4da245afd4b56e36dc745965f2f328a350af4c9e67f3d0fabb0fcd6:"
        }
      ]
    }
